From: OpenWrt EHR330 support <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: use upstream SerDes sequence on EHR330

Keep the RTL8221B-VB-CG C45 config_init callback: omitting it leaves
possible_interfaces and rate_matching unset and relies on bootloader state.

On EHR330, finish after the upstream RTL822xB SerDes option-mode sequence.
The additional OpenWrt ALDPS/SGMII-AN/restart tail is absent from upstream
Linux v6.19 and its self-clearing-bit poll times out on this board. The
reset retry cannot recover it without confirmed reset GPIO wiring.

Retain MDIO broadcast disable, mode selection, interface advertisement,
rate matching and propagation of MDIO write errors. Other boards retain
the existing OpenWrt sequence. Hardware DHCP/traffic validation is required.

Reference: https://codebrowser.dev/linux/linux/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c.html

--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -1310,6 +1310,9 @@ static int rtl822x_set_serdes_option_mode
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (!gen1 && of_machine_is_compatible("emplus,ehr330"))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (of_property_read_bool(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node, "realtek,aldps-enable"))
 		ret = phy_set_bits_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND1, RTL8221B_PHYCR1,
 				 RTL8221B_PHYCR1_ALDPS_EN | RTL8221B_PHYCR1_ALDPS_XTAL_OFF_EN);
-- 
